      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Returning to the bag itself—the CELINE Triomphe handbag was originally designed by former creative director Hedi Slimane in 2018. It revisits the vintage \"Triomphe\" clasp from CELINE's early 1970s archives and retains the classic rectangular silhouette of Phoebe Philo's Classic Box bag.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/fvvvko0/31281373e4ed4e30.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/fvvvko0/0573be757ad1b4e5.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"Triomphe\" means \"triumph\" in French, referencing the Arc de Triomphe. Both the name and design details are a re-exploration of the brand's history—in 1972, founder Céline Vipiana's car broke down near the Arc de Triomphe. While waiting for help, she noticed the chain links surrounding the square and was struck by inspiration, conceiving the two interlocking C's of the Chain Blason logo—the prototype of the Triomphe emblem.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/fvvvko0/53b01dd71f9cb80f.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/fvvvko0/53b01dd71f9cb80f.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
